Two things to get right if you use it:

  1. confidence: "unknown" is NOT a negative result. It means the value was not
     measured. The evidence object says why. Rendering it as "no" turns our
     honesty into your misinformation.

  2. Show measured_at wherever you show a value. A fact about a Korean sign-up
     flow has a shelf life; the timestamp is what makes it usable.

